  "id": "COMPOUND:27344 - PROTEIN:5839",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between 7-Deacetyl-7-benzoylepoxyazadiradione and U251, mediated through the thioredoxin, mitochondrial pathway. This compound is implicated in targeting thioredoxin, a protein involved in cellular redox regulation, and this target is in turn engaged by oleamide and isodaucene, both of which are also linked to U251. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway, including a long-chain fatty acid derivative, indicates a potential mechanism of action that involves the modulation of redox-sensitive processes in mitochondria. The integration of these targets suggests that 7-Deacetyl-7-benzoylepoxyazadiradione may exert its effects through a pathway that involves the redox regulation of thioredoxin, which in turn influences cellular processes in U251. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and U251, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
